       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Higher doses mostly add side effects, such as peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they add little blood pressure benefit. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWould you like me to do one of these?\n1. **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter a lower starting dose**, such as 5 mg once daily, if the patient is new to amlodipine. You can titrate up from there.\n3. **Enter 20 mg as written**, if the dose is intentional. I'd add a note with your rationale, for example that it's a specialist-directed regimen.\n\nIf the goal is more blood pressure control beyond 10 mg, adding a second agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, is usually preferred over going above the maximum.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
